# UI boundary contract — what V3 serves, and what the kept interface must rebuild to read it

Spec-pack artifact 3 of 4 (DR-001) · Mission REQ-V3-GREENFIELD-R1
Authoring ticket: [`../wayfinder/issues/16-ui-flex-negotiation.md`](../wayfinder/issues/16-ui-flex-negotiation.md)
Authority: [`../wayfinder/decisions-ledger.md`](../wayfinder/decisions-ledger.md) — governing ruling **DR-048**
Factual substrate (read-only): [`../research/01-ui-boundary-contract.md`](../research/01-ui-boundary-contract.md)
Vocabulary: [`../wayfinder/GLOSSARY.md`](../wayfinder/GLOSSARY.md)
Status: draft. Not accepted until three lenses review, the orchestrator merges, and V accepts (DR-006).

---

## 0. How to read this document

**What this document is.** V3 is a new reasoning engine in a new repository. Its
web interface is *not* new: V ruled that the existing interface survives
(D-KEEP-V2-UI). But V also ruled how it survives, and the how is the whole
subject of this document.

**The governing ruling, in one paragraph.** DR-048: **no adapter.** Nothing
translates V3's output back into the old engine's shapes. The interface keeps its
*components and its user experience* — the pages, the canvas, the drawer, the
badges, the way a person moves through an answer — and **rebuilds its data layer**
against V3's own way of speaking, from the first day. The ten backend surfaces the
interface never called, and the split front door it was served through, **die**.
And all nine **honesty surfaces** — the places where the engine admits what it does
not know, where a number came from, and what it skipped — **flex**: the old
contract genuinely cannot express them, so the shapes are drawn fresh here.

**Words a stranger needs**, one line each:

- **Surface** — one address the interface can call, plus the shape that comes back.
  "`GET /api/debates/{id}` returns a debate" is a surface.
- **Data layer** — the code between the network and the screen: the fetching, the
  types, the joining, the state machines. This is what is rebuilt. The screens are
  not.
- **Serve-composition** — V3's way of producing served words (DR-044): the machine
  assembles **every computed fact** into one structured bundle; **one** model writes
  the text a person reads, honoring those facts; a **second** model judges whether
  the text matches the facts; the machine enforces that judgment. So every answer
  has three parts on the wire: the **fact bundle**, the **composed text**, and the
  **conformance verdict**. The interface reads all three.
- **Honesty surface** — a place where the answer tells on itself: "I abstained, and
  this is which kind of abstention"; "this number is reasoning, not measurement";
  "this branch was skipped because the budget ran out". Nine of them are named by
  DR-048 and each gets a row in section 4.
- **Flex** — a shape the interface must gain because the old one cannot carry the
  meaning. Ticket 16's standing guard is that flex is for outputs the old contract
  **genuinely** cannot express; DR-048 found that all nine honesty surfaces are such
  outputs (see contradiction C2).
- **Death list** — surfaces that do not enter V3's interface contract at all.
- **DRAFT—V RULES** — a stamp on any cell of this document where a real choice about
  what a person sees is still open. Those are V's, not this document's.

**What this document is not.** It is not endpoint design. It names the *resources*,
the *fields they must carry*, and the *events the interface must be able to hear* —
in requirements language. Whether that is REST, GraphQL, one document or twelve, is
the ARCHITECTURE loop's to propose and V's to ratify there (DR-005, as narrowed by
DR-024).

**How to check a claim here.** Sentences describing today's interface carry a
citation into [`../research/01-ui-boundary-contract.md`](../research/01-ui-boundary-contract.md)
(cited as `research/01 §X`), which itself carries `file:line` citations into the
frozen V2 engine. Sentences stating what V3 **must** do carry a decision record
(`DR-NNN`). A normative sentence with neither is a defect in this document; raise it
at review.

---

## 1. The native contract, at requirements level

### 1.1 The shape the serve-composition layer forces

DR-044 rejected pure render — "defeats the purpose of our design" — and settled the
serving architecture: machine facts in, one composed text out, a conformance verdict
over the pair, machine enforcement of that verdict. That single ruling determines the
shape of everything the interface reads:

1. **The facts and the prose are separate objects that travel together.** The
   interface never parses prose to learn a fact. Every badge, marker, and label in
   section 4 is driven by a typed field in the fact bundle; the composed text is
   display, never data.
2. **The conformance verdict is part of the payload.** A composition the judge
   rejected is either recomposed or flagged as a defect (DR-044). Either way the
   interface can see which happened. There is no silent serve.
3. **Every number arrives with its origin and its replay handle** — D4 (serving
   scores without their origin labels) is an indicted defect, and DR-034's replay law
   forbids serving a number V3 cannot recompute from frozen records with no model in
   the replay.

### 1.2 The resources

Requirements-level. Each entry names what the resource **must be able to carry**;
field names are illustrative, not normative.

**The six read on every answer:**

| Resource | Must carry |
|---|---|
| **Answer** | question line as asked; verdict band and verdict state; confidence band; the **typed abstention** if any, with its price cell (DR-012); **staleness state** (DR-015/016); **execution marks** (DR-021); **value hinges** (DR-017); **memory disclosure** (DR-044 Q61); composed text; **conformance verdict** + enforcement outcome; a handle to the run's execution-ledger digest (DR-027); the graph's root pointer |
| **Node** | claim text; **way of knowing** ∈ LOOKED_UP / RAN / REASONING (GLOSSARY; DR-040 Q22 forces the REASONING relabel when output is irreproducible); base score and final strength, each with a provenance reference; **defeater state**; **exploration state** (DR-016); node-scoped abstention; node-scoped execution marks; a stranger-readable restatement of itself (R9, DR-018 — every node individually restatable) |
| **Edge** | `from` node, `to` node, **relation** (supports / attacks / defeats / shared-crux), **strength**, provenance reference. Edges are first-class citizens of the payload, not implied by nesting (DR-022 as narrowed by DR-035; DR-030 J2 "ONE GRAPH") |
| **Fact bundle** | the complete set of machine facts handed to the composition model for this answer, addressable so the interface can show any fact the prose refers to (DR-044). This is the honesty surfaces' data source |
| **Composition record** | composed text; which facts it claims; the conformance judge's verdict; what the machine did about it (accepted / recomposed / defect-flagged) |
| **Provenance record** | per number and per claim: who or what produced it, from which inputs, with a locator (DR-044 Q51's locator gate is blocking), the method, and a **replay handle** (DR-034) |

**The rest of the contract:**

| Resource | Must carry |
|---|---|
| **Ask** | the question; run parameters that are the asker's dial (depth, agent count — DR-019); **risk tier** ∈ casual / standard / high-stakes (DR-011); decision/action owner, caller scope, `as_of` (DR-021 per-run ownership); steering pre-sets |
| **Typed abstention** | which kind — the battery's five (not searched / searched and found nothing / measured and inconclusive / not runnable / a value choice) as the **seeded** vocabulary, with the machine enforcing exactly one per open unknown (DR-044 Q55); the price cell (question class × risk tier, DR-011/012); the unlock condition |
| **Value hinge** | criteria and their sources; option vectors; the Pareto set; `weight_source` ∈ owner_elicited / org_policy / none — **with no `default` member** (DR-017); owner; the **reversal point**; the band on each side of it; visibly-served rejected criteria (DR-043) |
| **Memory disclosure** | whether a prior run was matched, the tier and relation, the prior run's own staleness state, the agreed/disagreed fields (the *difference statement*), what payload was pulled, **candidates found but not linked**, and an unlink control (DR-044 Q61; shape from `research/34-cross-run-memory.md` §1.8) |
| **Execution mark** | a typed record that something was not done normally, scoped to the answer or to a node: SKIPPED_BY_BUDGET (DR-021 knob 9), unresolved-type fallback label (DR-021 knob 10), DEGRADED DIVERSITY (DR-041), independent-critique-unavailable (DR-014), UNFALSIFIED-AFTER-ROTATION (DR-041), refused cycle / shared-crux redirect (DR-042), off-subject downgrade (DR-009), amended search terms (DR-008) |
| **Investigation** | the gap; its typed verdict (including UNINSTRUMENTED, which **blocks** the fairness claim); the remediation layer — why the gap exists, the effort grade, and the machine-constructed prompt for the next model — **openly marked model-authored and biased**, never replacing the verdict; whether user input is accepted (DR-045) |
| **Steering record** | menu selections plus **verbatim** free-text annotations, typed as human-steer input and disclosed in the served trail (DR-019) |
| **Execution-ledger digest** | everything executed — attempts, failures, could-not-dos — visible to the asker, with algorithm behavior consistent with the record (DR-027) |
| **Replay trail** | for any served number: the frozen records and the recomputation, with no model in the replay (DR-034) |
| **Model scorecard read** | per-model capability and bias facts derived from measured outcomes, and the model ledger's session record (DR-039, DR-046) |
| **Deployment register** | V3's own flag/config set, drawn fresh and V-ratified (DR-023) — not V2's |

### 1.3 The event stream

V3 emits a progress stream. Requirements on it, not its encoding:

**Event families.** Run lifecycle (accepted, planning, running, terminal-with-typed-
kind); node lifecycle (spawned, generating, text delta, complete, failed with a typed
reason, retrying with the attempt count against DR-020's cap of 2 regeneration
rounds); **graph** events (edge added with its relation; cycle refused and redirected
to a shared-crux node — DR-042 makes "circular dependency found" *served information*);
**serve-composition** events (fact bundle frozen, composition started, composition
delta, conformance verdict returned, recompose or defect flag — DR-044); **honesty**
events (abstention typed, budget skip marked, fallback labeled, investigation gap
opened, memory link decided, staleness trigger fired, branch marked UNDER-EXPLORED);
and **ledger** events (each executed attempt, failure, and could-not-do, per DR-027).

**Four laws on the stream**, each written against a named V2 failure:

- **E1 — No emitted event without a declared consumer.** V2 emits 18+ event names the
  interface never listens to and listens for 12 (`research/01 §C`). Charter clause 4
  (DR-047) — nothing shipped is unreachable — applies to the event vocabulary.
- **E2 — One name per meaning, declared once.** V2 emits `synthesis_completed` on the
  v2 path while the interface listens for `synthesis_complete`, which only the v1 path
  emits; the consequence is that **v2 debates never stream prose to the browser at all**
  (`research/01 §C`). Names are contract.
- **E3 — An event's payload is used or not sent.** V2's `tree_ready` carries the whole
  serialized debate and the interface throws it away, then refetches (`research/01 §C`).
- **E4 — The stream survives terminality.** V2 closes the stream permanently once a
  debate is complete or failed (`debateTerminal`, `research/01 §7`), which is exactly
  when DR-015's wake-ups and DR-016's revivals act. See flex row 4.

### 1.4 Contract-wide laws

These bind every resource above. Each replaces a specific V2 behavior the substrate
recorded.

| # | Law | Replaces |
|---|---|---|
| **L1** | **No unlabeled number.** Every served number carries its origin. No judgment and no magnitude ⇒ no number, ever — a typed visible record instead (DR-028) | D4; V2's four fallback variants |
| **L2** | **Every number carries a replay handle** and is recomputable from frozen records with no model in the replay (DR-034, DR-027) | trusted-run reconstruction that reached no pixel |
| **L3** | **Open vocabularies, seeded.** Any typed vocabulary the interface renders must degrade by showing the unknown label's raw text, never by rendering nothing. V2 has both patterns: `VerdictBanner` falls back to the raw band string (good); `caveats` is a hardcoded two-branch `if` where an unknown code renders **nothing** (`research/01 §4`) | closed unions on both sides of the wire |
| **L4** | **Reason text is never parsed.** Machine-readable state travels as a typed field; free text is display-only. V2 sniffs free-text `reason` for "provider"/"model"/"token"/"credential"/"auth"/"api key" and compares against one exact lowercase sentence (`research/01 §Abstentions`) | `looksProviderOrTokenRequired`, `isMissingJudgeOutputReason`, and the 401/403 substring match |
| **L5** | **One transport.** Server-side rendering and the browser read the same contract through the same front door. V2 has two mutually exclusive proxies plus a third path where SSR bypasses both (`research/01 §D`) | the dual-transport seam (section 3) |
| **L6** | **No served field without a consumer; no consumer without a served field.** Both directions of drift are defects (DR-047 clause 4) | V2's served-and-unread (`evidencePresence`, `argument_claim`, `score_provenance`, `judge_disagreements`, `score_caps`) and declared-but-never-served (`lens`, `score`, `scoring`) |
| **L7** | **Facts and prose travel together, with the verdict.** A defect-flagged composition is never served as if it were clean (DR-044) | — (new) |
| **L8** | **Degradation is typed.** Rate limiting, timeouts, and partial results arrive as typed states, not as thrown strings. Every public interface surface in V2 is IP-rate-limited and the interface has **no** 429 handling — `apiFetch` throws the body text as a generic `Error` (`research/01 §D`) | untyped failure |
| **L9** | **Every answer names its abstention cell** (DR-012) and every value-decided segment names whose weights decided it (DR-017) | silence |

