## 25. Open tensions and input contradictions — listed, never resolved

Recorded so a reviewer can see them rather than rediscover them. **This document
does not resolve any of them.** Items 1–5 are ledger-internal; items 6–8 are
packet-level staleness that a reader consulting an older artifact would hit.

1. **DR-025's row text still commissions a capture that nothing produces.** It
   reads *"V2 is captured AS PRODUCTION SHIPPED … for behavioral specs, golden
   vectors, and the race."* DR-033 part 4 closed the vector recorder as out of
   scope, and DR-047 retires the race and narrows DR-025 to "reference-capture
   definition" in its `supersedes` field — but **DR-025's own text is unamended and
   its `supersedes` field is untouched**, so a reader consulting DR-025 alone would
   still commission golden vectors for a race that no longer exists.

2. **DR-026 carries a vector-marking clause that DR-033 does not name.** DR-026
   says *"vectors mark the constant-1.0 path MUST-DIFFER."* DR-033 kills the
   MUST-MATCH/MUST-DIFFER vector class and its `supersedes` field names **DR-028's**
   vector-marking clause and DR-003's equivalence clause — **not DR-026's**. Two
   rows of the same kind were treated differently.

3. **DR-024's recorder clause is annotated as overtaken but not superseded by
   anything.** The row carries an in-place bracket — *"[Recorder clause OVERTAKEN by
   DR-033…]"* — while DR-033's `supersedes` field does not name DR-024. The
   annotation is a reading aid, not a supersession record.

4. **Two DR status fields still read as pending after their successors landed.**
   DR-038 is `FINAL (Q34 pending)` though **DR-045 closed Q34**; DR-042 is
   `FINAL (Q50 pending)` though **DR-043 closed Q50**. A third — DR-044's
   `FINAL (Q61 mechanism pending)` with the condition *"mechanism details pending
   research ticket 34"* — is **partly** stale: research 34 has delivered, so the
   research is no longer pending, but **V's ruling on its 24 questions is**. The
   three fields are not distinguishable as written.

5. **Two V-owned register parameters lost their owner when ticket 15 was
   transformed.** DR-047 retires the race and transforms ticket 15, which owned
   **`stage11Rollout`** and **`adoptionBar`**. `adoptionBar` is dissolved *by
   implication* — DR-047 removes the adoption bar, the matched-cost law and the
   promotion question — but **no DR names the parameter**. **`stage11Rollout` is
   named by no DR at all** and is the one register row in §4 with no V value
   (§23 `OD-S-01`). A parameter the enforcement machinery is built to catch as
   unresolved should not be the one nobody owns.

6. **A ratified label may flip under a knob that was ratified separately.** DR-031
   ratified **Q27 as the battery's single `LLM` row**. DR-020 knob 8 says coverage
   *"becomes a gate only after outcome data sets the threshold"* — and a gate is
   code acting on the model's answer, which under **DR-037's label law makes the row
   HYBRID**. Today the rows are consistent (a diagnostic note is stored, not acted
   on); **no DR says whether the label follows the knob when the gate activates.**

7. **The glossary still describes the race as live.** `../wayfinder/GLOSSARY.md`
   reads *"The race — V3 must beat frozen V2 on measures declared and frozen BEFORE
   the first run (ticket 15)"*, and its **Golden vectors** entry still describes
   MUST-MATCH / MUST-DIFFER / UNPINNED with *"zero UNPINNED is a spec-readiness
   gate"*. DR-047 retires the race; DR-033 dissolves the vector framework. The
   glossary is the stranger-facing entry point, so this is the most reader-visible
   staleness in the packet.

8. **The carryover manifest (revision 2) predates DR-036 … DR-048.** It still
   describes V2 as *"the race's control arm"* (§1, §12.1 part 2, §12.3 item 3, §16
   item 2) and routes **`OD-13` (verdict bands) to ticket 15**, which DR-047
   transformed — this spec carries that row as `OD-C-01` under artifact 4 instead.
   The manifest's normative organ content is unaffected; its **race framing and one
   owner column** are stale.

