### 12.4 Open V3 spec decisions

The first draft's UNPINNED register was a list of vector marks that could not be authored. With the
MUST-MATCH class dead, the *marks* are moot but the *substance* is not: these are real design
questions this manifest cannot answer, each now stated as an open V3 spec decision. **OD-NN replaces
the draft's UP-NN one for one**, plus one new row (OD-23) surfaced by DR-030 and DR-035.

**The successor readiness gate:** this artifact closes when **every row below has a ruling**. That is
DR-004's coverage law applied to this artifact — no row left contested-silent — and it replaces the
retired zero-UNPINNED gate. **22 rows are open today.**

| Row | Open decision | Where it bites | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|
| **OD-01** | **Cardinality policy.** Uncapped counting controlled only by cluster collapse, top-k per polarity (and what k), or a cardinality-insensitive aggregator? Stake: six mediocre supporters at 0.30 aggregate to 0.882 and nearly beat one strong supporter at 0.900; a cardinality-insensitive operator would break the two literature vectors and require re-derivation (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` S2, Q4). | §4.2f–g | **25** (cross-ref 23, which owns Q45) |
| **OD-02** | **Interior unjudged nodes.** M1 is unambiguous for a leaf. For an interior node with judged descendants: **transparent** (children's arrows lift to the nearest judged ancestor), **subtree excluded**, or **τ derived from children** under a declared rule? The third reintroduces a computed-from-nothing base score (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` Q1). | §4.2e | **25** (cross-ref 21) |
| **OD-03** | **Perspective containers in the one graph.** Does a perspective node carry its own claim and its own arrow, or is it a pure grouping node that emits none? V2's two variants disagree by 0.96875 versus 0.5 on exactly this (§10.2). | §6.2, §6.3 | **21** (Q26) |
| **OD-04** | **Contradicted evidence after D1(d).** The verifier reports contradiction **without a magnitude**, by its own schema. Does V3 emit no arrow, a typed unknown-magnitude attacker that cannot contribute strength, or extend the verifier to report a magnitude it can vouch for? | §6.3 | **22** |
| **OD-05** | **Tie case and identity element under strict-and.** Under accumulate, `va == vs` returns exactly τ and the identity element is zero. The strict-and operator's tie behavior and identity are undefined. | §4.2b, §4.2f | **25** |
| **OD-06** | **Free arrow strengths.** The labeled-arrow idea carries (DR-035). Is a *freely settable* arrow strength admitted beyond M3's cluster gate, or is the strength only ever the gate's output? The research found no factor requiring it that is not already expressible as a τ cap or a cluster gate (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` "what to add later", item 4). | §4.2c, §4.2g | **25** (cross-ref 22) |
| **OD-07** | **Abstention arithmetic.** At what fraction of abstained children does a parent **refuse** to emit a number at all? V2's answer was an aggregate band gate that still printed the raw number underneath, which D1 forbids (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` Q8). | §4.4, §9.2e | **25** |
| **OD-08** | **Semantic restatement: gate or flag, and at what threshold.** Does D3's clause bind paraphrases whose provenance genuinely differs, or only same-provenance restatement (which M3 already collapses)? If it may gate: the threshold, a complete-linkage requirement, and within-polarity/within-parent scoping. Named risks: transitive branch collapse, polarity collision, and two-sided gaming — including posting a near-duplicate of the strongest counter-argument to get it absorbed and silenced (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` S6, Q5). | §4.2i, §10.3 | **22** (cross-ref 25) |
| **OD-09** | **Provenance key width.** Which fields make two evidence items "the same family": source domain, publisher, underlying study or dataset, retrieval-query lineage, producing model family, producing run? Named the single highest-leverage V value in the structural half — it is what converts 0.784 back into 0.400 (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` Q3). | §4.2g, §10.3 | **22** |
| **OD-10** | **Operator fallback.** When no operator is declared for a parent: refuse to emit a parent number and serve components only (the upstream default), or a declared fallback operator that is printed? (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` Q6.) | §4.2f | **25** (cross-ref 23) |
| **OD-11** | **The Leans meter's admission rule.** V2's gate — "any coverage above zero" — dies with D1 and D4. Does V3 serve such a meter at all, and on what admission rule, given there are no default base scores left to dilute it? | §9.2e | **24** (cross-ref 16) |
| **OD-12** | **Way-of-knowing ceilings.** Three numeric ceilings for looked-up / ran / reasoned, **or** a band rule only with no numeric cap? A band rule alone is cleaner and harder to game; numbers are more expressive and more arguable (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` Q2, M4). | §4.2h | **22** (cross-ref 24, which owns Q51) |
| **OD-13** | **Verdict band thresholds.** V2's supported/unsupported boundaries are declared constants, honestly versioned. V3's are a fresh design and interact with DR-012's abstention-price matrix. | §9.2, §5 | **15** (routed to ticket 15's sitting; not a theme row) |
| **OD-14** | **A value-conditional verdict state.** Does the shadow-mode precedent generalize into a served `value_conditional` state, and may a winner ever be served on a value weight (with the reversal point printed) or must comparisons always be handed back? DR-017 ruled the flows, not the state vocabulary (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` R2, Q12). | §9.2f–g | **25** (Q50) |
| **OD-15** | **Which abstention kind.** The battery names five typed abstentions. Which one a judge-unavailable, unparseable, or refusing node carries — and whether the kind differs per cause — is unwritten for the scoring organ. | §5.4, §10.1 | **24** (Q55) |
| **OD-16** | **Claim-typing disposition.** Does V3's claim-type, scope and ambiguity extraction stay fully deterministic (a MACHINE row — a zero-model-call prohibition with a test) or become HYBRID? The label decides what the spec **forbids**, not merely what it permits. | §5.2a | **19** |
| **OD-17** | **The argument-only branch set.** V2 drops the evidence term for exactly two claim types. Whether V3 keeps that closed set — and whether value-laden claims join it, given DR-017's value flows — is unruled. | §5.2f | **19** (cross-ref 25) |
| **OD-18** | **Which node states enter the scored graph**, and does the debug facet use the same set? V2 disagrees with itself here; V3 needs one rule for both surfaces or an explicit served divergence. | §6.4, §9.3 | **21** |
| **OD-19** | **The SPLIT child and arrow-kind vocabulary.** V2 has two child shapes (support, challenge). SPLIT needs necessary conditions, sub-questions, assumptions, scope carve-outs and defeaters, and the arrow needs at least the rebut/undercut distinction. | §6.3, §7.2e | **21** (Q26) |
