## 16. Open tensions and unresolved input contradictions

Listed, never resolved. Four of revision 1's items are **closed** by the new rulings — the UP-13/UP-21
routing, the DR-025-versus-DR-027 dead-check tension (DR-032), the MUST-MATCH reading of DR-023
(DR-033 removes the need for a reading at all), and the trusted-run property-or-procedure question
(DR-034: both) — and the D3 scope question moved into OD-08 under theme 22. What remains, plus what
the new rulings created:

1. **DR-024's recorder clause is now stale, and DR-033 does not name it.** DR-024 reads: *"the vector
   recorder (ticket 27) is the sole scoring-ground-truth source."* DR-033 part 4 closes ticket 27 as
   out of scope. DR-033's `supersedes` field names only DR-028's vector-marking clause and DR-003's
   equivalence-testing clause — **not** DR-024. The ledger therefore carries a live sentence pointing
   at a closed ticket; a reader consulting DR-024 alone would still commission the recorder.

2. **DR-025's "golden vectors" purpose has no referent, and DR-033 does not name it either.** DR-025
   reads: *"V2 is captured AS PRODUCTION SHIPPED … for behavioral specs, golden vectors, and the
   race."* With the recorder out of scope nothing captures V2 for vectors, and DR-033 part 2
   describes the control arm as **measured end-to-end at race time, as-is** — run, not captured. Two
   questions follow that this manifest cannot answer: is V2 still *frozen* in any form for the race
   (a build, a pinned checkout, a recorded transcript), or run live from `main` at race time? And who
   owns freezing it — ticket 15, or nobody? DR-025's own `supersedes` field is untouched.

3. **DR-003's condition field still reads as live.** DR-003's `conditions` column says *"golden
   vectors protect equivalence."* DR-033 supersedes that clause in part while DR-033's own text says
   the clean-room re-specification stands. The decision text and the condition text on the same row
   now point in different directions.

4. **DR-032's "must demonstrably fire" has no stated bar, and this manifest declined to invent one.**
   §12.2 (P-D5) records the requirement and marks the bar unruled. Candidates: "fires at least once
   against real spreads"; "fires at a rate consistent with observed spreads"; or the upstream rule-12
   standard for gates — *"every gate must be shown to fire both ways before adoption"*
   (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` Q5). The choice changes what launch has to demonstrate.

5. **The organ↔stage table is vetoable.** DR-030 records its derived organ↔stage table as vetoable at
   review. Section 3 reproduces it as given. Any lens that disagrees with a stage assignment is
   disagreeing with a derivation, not with a ruling.

6. **DR-035 leaves loop handling behind while DR-030 makes loops possible.** Consistent as written,
   but together they open a gap nobody has closed: V3's graph can contain cycles for the first time
   (defeaters may target non-parents), the experiment's loop handling is explicitly not carried, and
   DF-QuAD requires acyclicity. Recorded as an open decision (**OD-23**, new in this revision) rather
   than chosen. Flagged here as well because it is a consequence of two rulings rather than a
   leftover from research.

7. **No ruling names the successor readiness gate.** The ticket's original Definition of Done made
