## 12. V3's test base — and V2 as reference only

### 12.1 The governing ruling (DR-033)

V ruled: *"nothing from V3 must match V2; starting fresh, never look back at what was already
debated; V2 serves as reference; V3 must be much better."* The cascade, each part vetoable by V:

1. **The MUST-MATCH class is dead.** V2 output conformance is not a V3 requirement anywhere.
2. **V2 remains the race's control arm** (DR-025 untouched), measured **end-to-end at race time,
   as-is**. That is ticket 15's layer and is deliberately not this artifact's.
3. **V3's math is tested against literature vectors plus V3-spec property tests.** The D1–D5
   prohibitions become **properties of V3 itself** — no invented numbers, real weighting — testable
   without any V2 vector.
4. **Ticket 27, the V2 vector recorder, is out of scope.** Its premise — protect equivalence with V2
   — is void, and divergence is sanctioned. The nine capture requirements this manifest's first draft
   carried are retired with it.
5. **This section reworks** to "V3 self-test base plus V2 as reference".

DR-003's clean-room re-specification **stands**; what died is only the obligation to reproduce V2's
outputs. DR-033 supersedes DR-028's vector-marking clause and DR-003's equivalence-testing clause in
part.

### 12.2 The four layers of V3's test base

**Layer 1 — external ground truth.** The two published literature vectors (§4.5), reproduced
exactly, plus the properties of the DF-QuAD arithmetic as property tests over generated graphs:
determinism; an added attacker strictly lowers; an added supporter strictly raises; empty gives
empty; an isolated node gives its own τ. These are the authors' numbers, not V2's, and they carry
zero contamination.

**Layer 2 — the defect prohibitions, as properties of V3.** Each replaces a MUST-DIFFER vector mark
with something stronger: a rule that must hold for *every* input, checkable with no V2 artifact
present.

| Property | Statement | How it is checked |
|---|---|---|
| **P-D1** | No code path can produce a base score in the absence of a judgement. | Generate graphs with arbitrary unjudged subsets; assert no number exists for an unjudged node, and that each parent's value equals the value computed from its judged children alone — §4.2e's identity-element argument makes this exactly checkable. |
| **P-D2** | The engine and operator identifier is an input to every run, emitted by the component that computed it; no production selection path reads a literal. | Assert both operators are computable on demand and produce different recorded identifiers; assert the identifier travels with the result; assert that where the rival operator flips the band, both readings appear (DR-031 makes this spec law via Q47). |
| **P-D3** | Counting is by provenance: N restatements sharing a provenance key contribute exactly once, at the strongest member. | Property test over generated sibling sets — the 0.784 → 0.400 collapse computed from V3's own arithmetic. Plus: the restatement flag appears for same-meaning, different-provenance siblings and changes no number. |
| **P-D4** | Every weight-bearing number in a served payload carries its own kind, source and producer; no payload-level label may be contradicted by a per-item fact. | Assert a number with no provenance is unservable; assert a mixed-freshness payload reports freshness per item; fuzz payload assembly for aggregate labels that contradict item facts. |
| **P-D5** | Judge weight is a function of recorded outcomes, and the learned path is reachable. | Feed recorded outcomes; assert at least one judge's weight moves. A weight constant under all outcome histories fails. Paired with **DR-032**: the disagreement flag must **demonstrably fire** on V3's own data — the exact bar is unruled and flagged in section 16. |

**Layer 3 — house-rule gates.** Each of H1–H8 (section 11) expressed as a standing test: the
provider-interface boundary; the second-provider configuration swap; **purity of the propagation
math** (also DR-034's precondition); operator swappability; the evidence-gated leaf; source
anonymization before a role reads prior turns; the skeptic's no-unaddressed-attack certification as a
serving precondition; and cost as a tie-breaker rather than a driver.

**Layer 4 — battery and law gates.** The rulings that are directly checkable:

- **DR-034 replay** — a continuous self-test that every servable number recomputes from frozen
  records with no model in the path, plus the **launch ceremony**: one independent replay of recorded
  runs that must pass exactly. A launch acceptance criterion, not a development convenience.
- **DR-027 ledger completeness** — every executed thing has a row; the digest is user-visible; no
  served sentence implies a check the ledger says did not run.
- **DR-018/DR-019 stranger coverage** — load-bearing nodes exhaustively restatable, sampling derived
  from the asker's run parameters, ratcheting on failure.
- **DR-017 overlay detachment** — recompute every strength with the value overlay detached and assert
  byte-identity. The research asks for this to be an enforced invariant rather than a convention
  (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` §The invariant).
- **DR-012 / DR-009 / DR-014 / DR-030 knobs 9 and 10** — the abstention cell is named; an off-subject
  downgrade is visible; a missing second lineage caps, labels and records a lift path; every budget
  skip carries its marker; every unresolved type or field carries its label.

**Scenario coverage.** V3's property tests should exercise at least the shapes research/03
inventoried, now read as **test scenarios rather than recorded pairs**
(`../research/03-golden-vector-plan.md` §Vector families): single node; shallow-wide fans; deep
chains; realistic mixed graphs; degenerate and error graphs (cycle, missing endpoint, self-parent,
duplicates, out-of-range); container and pass-through shapes; evidence-verdict variants; base-score
extremes; the mediating-function tie boundary; arrow-strength extremes and conflicts; float
accumulation order; unjudged subsets; the dedup ladder from byte-identical through whitespace, case,
Unicode and paraphrase; judge-output duplication both byte-identical and one-byte-apart; abstention
and degradation paths; operator-selection variants; mixed-provenance payloads; the reducer's
compositions, caps, ladders and orderings; banding and suppression; and the normalizer's
classification, scope and ambiguity behavior. **None of these carries a V2 expected output.**

### 12.3 What V2 is still good for

Three uses, all reference (DR-033):

1. **The diseases.** Section 10's `file:line` evidence documents what went wrong and exactly where,
   so a designer can recognize the same shape in new code.
2. **Design source material.** The organ specifications in sections 4–9 were extracted from V2's
   observable behavior. That is where the designs came from; it is not what they are measured
   against.
3. **The race's control arm.** V2 is run end-to-end at race time, as-is, by ticket 15 (DR-025,
   DR-033 part 2). That is an end-to-end product comparison, not an organ-level conformance test —
   the two layers were separated deliberately (`../wayfinder/map.md` §Race layering).

**Not a use:** any conformance test, anywhere, at any level.

