## 4. Organ 1 — the scoring engine (re-specified DF-QuAD / QBAF)

### 4.1 Purpose

Take a graph of claims — each carrying a base score that a judge actually produced — plus the
labeled arrows between them, and produce one number per claim: how strongly the graph supports
it. Attackers pull a claim down; supporters push it up; the arithmetic is published and fixed.
This number is the quantitative basis of the served answer, and under DR-030 (J1) it is the
**only** scoring math in V3: WEIGH and COMPOSE share it, so there is one set of receipts rather
than two.

### 4.2 Exact behavior

**(a) The aggregation function α ("probabilistic sum").** For a list of incoming strengths
(`../research/02-scoring-behavior-spec.md` §1.2; DF-QuAD as published):

```
agg([])         = 0
agg(v1 … vn)    = 1 − Π(1 − vi)
```

Computed as a left fold `a ← 1 − (1−a)(1−v)` from `a = 0`. This is commutative in exact
arithmetic but **not** bit-identical under reordering in IEEE-754 doubles, so V3's arrow order
must be deterministic and recorded — not to match anything, but so that V3's own replay (DR-034)
is exact.

**(b) The mediating function σ.** Given a node's τ, aggregated attacker strength `va` and
aggregated supporter strength `vs`:

```
σ(τ, va, vs) = τ − τ·(va − vs)         if va ≥ vs
σ(τ, va, vs) = τ + (1 − τ)·(vs − va)   otherwise
```

The comparison is `≥`, not `>`. The tie case `va == vs` therefore returns exactly τ. This is what
makes DF-QuAD discontinuity-free; a V3 that used `>` would introduce the discontinuity the method
exists to avoid.

**(c) Labeled arrows are first-class objects** (DR-022 as narrowed by DR-035). An arrow is
`{source, target, polarity ∈ {support, attack}, strength ∈ [0,1], kind}`. Its strength is what
lets an arrow transmit less than the whole of its source's strength: a child's contribution to
its target is `arrow strength × strength(child)` before aggregation — the reading the V2
experiment used (`coordinator/app/qbaf/semantics.py:53`) and the one V3 adopts under DR-030 (J1).
Arrow identity is `(source, target, polarity)`; exact duplicates collapse; **the same identity
carrying two different strengths is a loud, typed integrity error and never a silent pick**. An
arrow may target a node that is **not** the source's structural parent — this is what makes a
defeater expressible at all, and V2 cannot do it
(`../research/04-node-graph-data-model.md` §A.2, §C).

**(d) Evaluation order.** Topological, over the union of support and attack arrows, so every
predecessor's strength is final before it is read. A node with no incoming arrows gets
`σ(τ, 0, 0) = τ`. A cycle is a typed error, never a partial result and never a fixed-point
approximation — but note that cycles become *constructible* in V3 for the first time (OD-23).

**(e) M1 — τ comes from judgement, or the node contributes nothing.** There is no default τ at any
layer (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` M1; DR-028). An unjudged node emits **no arrow** and
carries an explicit `ABSTAINED` record naming why. The arithmetic makes this exact rather than a
compromise: `agg([]) = 0` is the aggregation's identity element and `σ(τ, 0, 0) = τ`, so
**dropping an unjudged child's arrow leaves the parent on precisely the value its judged children
justify**. Interior unjudged nodes: OD-02.

**(f) M2 — the combination operator is declared per parent.** Two operators exist: *accumulate*
(the probabilistic sum above) and *strict-and* (the product). Which applies to a given parent's
children is declared by the SPLIT stage's conjunction structure — "what would **all** have to be
true" (`../research/04-node-graph-data-model.md` SPLIT gap 1;
`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` M2/S11). Where no operator is declared, the parent emits
**no number** and its components are served alone (fallback: OD-10). The magnitude is why this
outranks every weighting question here: on the mission's worked case — four sub-claims at 0.95,
0.60, 0.35, 0.50 — accumulate gives **0.9935** and strict-and gives **0.0997**, a **9.96×** gap.
Where the rival operator would flip the served band, **both readings are served with the deciding
choice printed** — never averaged, never an abstention. DR-031 ratifies **Q47 as a MACHINE row**:
computing what the other rule would have produced is machine work and is now spec law, not an
aspiration.

**(g) M3 — provenance cluster collapse.** Sibling support is partitioned by a declared provenance
key; **each cluster contributes once, at the strength of its strongest member**
(`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` M3). A gate, not a bonus: the aggregation already rewards
multiple supporters, so paying again for independence double-counts it. Computed effect on the
audit's worked case: three restatements of a 0.40 claim aggregate to 0.784 and contribute
**0.400** under cluster collapse. The partition is derivable; the **key width is a V policy
value** — OD-09.

**(h) M4 — way-of-knowing ceiling.** τ is capped by how the claim was known — LOOKED_UP / RAN /
REASONING — as a **ceiling, never a multiplier**, because a cap can only lower a number and can
never invent one. A reasoning-only root serves as a hypothesis plus a research plan, not as a
verdict. Ceiling values, or the choice of a band rule with no numbers: OD-12.

**(i) F1 — the semantic-restatement flag.** Where two siblings appear to say the same thing in
different words, the node and the wire carry `possible_restatement_of: [node_ids],
similarity: x.xx`. **It changes no number.** Whether it may ever gate: OD-08.

**(j) The value overlay never touches the graph** (DR-017). Value weights are a second layer
attaching at computed hinge nodes; τ, arrow strengths, strengths and provenance are computed with
no reference to any value weight. `weight_source ∈ {owner_elicited, org_policy, none}` — the set
has **no `default` member**, for the same reason there is no default τ. Every value-decided
segment carries a visible marker naming whose weights decided it. Flow A (serve the conditional
plus the reversal point) always runs; Flow B asks one swing question per real hinge; Flow C is
opt-in standing profiles.

**(k) Fragility and leverage are outputs, never weights** (DR-031 ratifies **Q46 and Q49 as
MACHINE rows**). Removal-based impact — recompute with a node dropped and report the difference —
produces the leverage ranking and the fragility table. Feeding sensitivity back into τ or arrow
strength is forbidden by construction: weights → strengths → sensitivity → weights is a loop with
no declared fixed point, and the engine could then be made to converge anywhere
(`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` S8).

### 4.3 Inputs and outputs

**Inputs.** A node set with per-node τ present *only* where a judge produced one; the labeled
arrow set; the per-parent operator declaration; the provenance partition; the way-of-knowing label
per node; and the run's recorded engine/operator identifier — an input, never a source literal
(section 10.2).

**Outputs.** A per-node record joining the number to its origin, never a flat `node_id → float`
map (`../research/32-weight-derivation.md` P1): at minimum
`{strength, tau_source, way_of_knowing, cluster_id, judged_by, abstained, supported_by,
attacked_by, operator_used}`. Plus the graph fingerprint, the operator identifier emitted **by the
computing component**, the leverage and fragility outputs (§4.2k), and a ledger row for every
computation (DR-027).

**Required fingerprint properties** (the idea is V2's, at
`coordinator/app/qbaf/debate_adapter.py:329-338`; the requirement is V3's): the digest is
**input-order-independent**, it **changes when any τ changes**, and it **differs between two
different operator selections on the same graph**. The last is what stops two runs under different
rules from being mistaken for each other.

### 4.4 Edge cases

| Situation | Required behavior |
|---|---|
| Empty node set | Empty result. Never a fabricated number. |
| Node with no incoming arrows | `strength = τ` |
| `va == vs` exactly | `strength = τ` (first σ branch) |
| τ outside `[0,1]` | Typed error at compute time |
| Arrow endpoint absent from the node set | Typed error at compute time |
| Cycle in support ∪ attack | Typed error; never a partial or fixed-point result (policy question: OD-23) |
| Duplicate identical arrow | Collapses once |
| Same arrow identity, two different strengths | Loud typed integrity error |
| Unknown node or arrow kind | **Loud failure.** V2 silently records an unmapped marker and disconnects a whole sub-tree from the root's score with no error (`../research/04-node-graph-data-model.md` §A.1) — the disease, not the design. |
| Node has no judgement | No arrow; typed `ABSTAINED` record; parent unaffected (DR-028) |
| All of a parent's children abstained | Parent refuses to emit a number (threshold: OD-07) |
| Any failure at all | Caught, typed, **and written to the ledger**. V2 swallows protocol-analysis exceptions with a print (`coordinator/app/protocol/runner.py:52-60`); under DR-027 a swallowed failure is a violation. |

### 4.5 The external ground truth this organ must satisfy

Two literature vectors are **published external ground truth, not V2 behavior**, and carry zero
clean-room contamination. Under DR-033 they are the *only* recorded input→output pairs V3 is
required to reproduce (`../research/03-golden-vector-plan.md`; transcribed in V2 at
`coordinator/tests/test_dfquad.py:95-138`, which is where they were found, not what they prove):

- **Literature vector 1** (arXiv:2307.13582 Fig. 3). All τ = 0.5; supports `B→A, C→A`; attacks
  `D→A, E→B, F→D, G→F, H→F`. Required: `F = 0.125`, `B = 0.25`, `D = 0.4375`, `A = 0.59375`;
  leaves `C, E, G, H = 0.5`.
- **Literature vector 2** (arXiv:2407.08497 Fig. 1). τ: `alpha 0.5, beta 0.3, gamma 0.6, rho 0.7,
  zeta 0.4`; supports `beta→alpha, zeta→gamma`; attacks `gamma→alpha, rho→beta`. Required:
  `zeta = 0.4`, `rho = 0.7`, `gamma = 0.76`, `beta = 0.09`, `alpha = 0.165`.

**Properties of the math** that V3 must also satisfy, as property tests over generated graphs
rather than as recorded pairs: determinism across repeated calls; adding an attacker strictly
lowers the target; adding a supporter strictly raises it; an empty graph gives an empty result; an
isolated node gives its own τ.

### 4.6 Battery stage owner

**WEIGH and COMPOSE** (DR-030 J1). One math, one set of receipts, both stages.

